  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Moyee/FairChain Child Future Proof Coffee Chains in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Moyee Coffee and FairChain Foundation in the Netherlands were established in 2012 in the Netherlands to make the coffee value chain fairer and provide coffee farmers with a decent living income.The aim of this project is:1.	Creation of a Living Income for smallholder farmers and labourers;2.	Engagement &amp; Ownership in the project by farmers, labourers, and other stakeholders;3.	Education programme focused on children of farmers and labourers;4.	Job creation programme in the coffee supply chain of Moyee/FairChain;5.	Transparent coffee chains showing progress of the project;6.	The impact of the local measures is monitored and adjusted where necessary.Internal implementation and transparency1.	Ensuring that Moyee/FairChain internal measures are aimed at countering and preventing child labour and implemented in their business.2.	Moyee/FairChain creates transparency and informs their customers and stakeholders about how the business reduces the risks of child labour in the chain.3.	Consumer engagement by letting consumers contribute to making the Moyee coffee supply chain child labour free and creating a future for children of farmers and labourers in the coffee supply chain.4.	In-house measures are being monitored and adjusted, where necessary.</narrative>
  </description>
